---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Get started" description="How to download, build and run Civ 1.5 Remastered.">
  <h1>Get started</h1>
  <p class="lead">Download the remaster, add the files of the original game, and play.</p>

  <h2>Play</h2>
  <ol class="plain-list">
    <li>
      Download the latest release from
      <a href="https://github.com/DavIT-Futures/Civ_1_5_Remastered/releases">GitHub Releases</a> and unpack it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Put the files of Civilization 1 for DOS in a folder named <code>CIVILIZATION</code> next to
      <code>Civ_1_5_Remastered.Desktop.exe</code>. The game files are not part of this project; a copy is on the
      Internet Archive:
      <a href="https://archive.org/download/CIVILIZATION_201902/CIVILIZATION.zip">CIVILIZATION.zip</a>
      (<a href="https://archive.org/details/CIVILIZATION_201902">item page</a>).
    </li>
    <li>Run <code>Civ_1_5_Remastered.Desktop.exe</code>.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Build from source</h2>
  <p>
    You need the <a href="https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download">.NET 10 SDK</a> and the <code>CIVILIZATION</code>
    folder next to <code>Civ_1_5_Remastered.sln</code>.
  </p>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/DavIT-Futures/Civ_1_5_Remastered.git
cd Civ_1_5_Remastered
dotnet build Civ_1_5_Remastered.sln
dotnet run --project Civ_1_5_Remastered.Desktop</code></pre>

  <h2>Keys</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Key</th><th>What it does</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>F11</code></td><td>Full screen on and off</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Alt+H</code></td><td>Help of the turn</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>All other keys work as in the original game.</p>

  <h2>Saved games</h2>
  <p>
    Saved games are the original <code>CIVIL0.SVE</code> – <code>CIVIL9.SVE</code> files, and the original game can
    load them. The hit points of damaged units are kept in a <code>.HP</code> file next to each save.
  </p>
</Layout>
